:12a9f17b4ca98acf059d678ba42098c73fd43e4c06591a3343a3fc9481f7128d","file":"preprints/Spectral-scalar-curvature-and-uniform-Urysohn-width-October-5-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":35,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"58648c980583aee6ad9adc87eb8a4c72c40732a4a7650096274e44787dd68261","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Spectral-scalar-curvature-and-uniform-Urysohn-width-October-5-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:12a9f17b4ca98acf059d678ba42098c73fd43e4c06591a3343a3fc9481f7128d","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Spectral-scalar-curvature-and-uniform-Urysohn-width-October-5-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L35"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every integer $n\\ge4$ there is a finite constant $C_n$ with the\nfollowing property. Every connected complete smooth Riemannian\n$n$-manifold $(M,g)$ without boundary satisfying\n\\eqref{eq:spectral-bound} admits a continuous map $f:M\\to K$ to a\nsimplicial complex of dimension at most $n-2$ such that\n\\[\n \\diam_g f^{-1}(y)\\le C_n\\qquad(y\\in K).\n\\]\nIn particular, $\\UW_{n-2}(M,g)\\le C_n$."}
